    <glyph id="cytosol" class="compartment">
      <label text="Cytosol" />
      <bbox x="37.33" y="252.72" w="411.61" h="112.24" />
    </glyph>
    <glyph id="mitochondrial_matrix" class="compartment">
      <label text="Mitochondrial matrix" />
      <bbox x="-12.28" y="402.96" w="510.83" h="99.44" />
    </glyph>
    <glyph id="cell" class="compartment">
      <label text="Cell" />
      <bbox x="12.57" y="540.40" w="461.12" h="99.44" />
    </glyph>
    <glyph id="FE_SUPPLY" class="simple chemical" compartmentRef="cytosol">
      <label text="Soil Fe / S availability" />
      <bbox x="162.73" y="0.00" w="160.80" h="34.64" />
      <glyph id="FE_SUPPLY__u0" class="unit of information">
        <label text="the NNMF evidence sits here" />
        <bbox x="168.73" y="-9.00" w="189.00" h="16.00" />
      </glyph>
      <extension>
        <qbo:annotation xmlns:qbo="https://dr-richard-barker.github.io/quantum-biology-atlas/qbo/1.0" entity="QBO:FE_SUPPLY" evidenceTier="T2" confidence="verified">
          <qbo:quantumClass>structural_context</qbo:quantumClass>
          <qbo:xref db="chebi">CHEBI:29033</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="chebi">CHEBI:29034</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="chebi">CHEBI:16189</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:evidence ref="Islam2020" doi="10.3389/fpls.2020.00325" direction="decrease" fieldRegime="NNMF">The geomagnetic field contributes to efficient iron uptake in Arabidopsis; reducing it to near-null affects root metal reductase activity.
</qbo:evidence>
          <qbo:evidence ref="Vigani2021" doi="10.3390/ijms221810166" direction="altered" fieldRegime="NNMF">Geomagnetic-field-dependent modulation of iron-sulfur interplay in Arabidopsis, most pronounced under combined Fe and S deficiency.
</qbo:evidence>
          <qbo:evidence ref="Narayana2018" doi="10.1016/j.lssr.2018.08.005" direction="altered" fieldRegime="NNMF">Reduction of the geomagnetic field to near-null affects Arabidopsis root mineral nutrition.
</qbo:evidence>
          <qbo:rationale>Note carefully what the cited work does and does not show. Islam 2020 and Vigani 2021 measured iron uptake and Fe-S interplay under altered field conditions — nutritional physiology. Neither measured cluster assembly. This entity is T2 because the field effect is demonstrated for the process it names; the assembly entities above remain T3 because that evidence does not reach them.
</qbo:rationale>
        </qbo:annotation>
      </extension>
    </glyph>
    <glyph id="FE_UPTAKE" class="complex" compartmentRef="plasma_membrane">
      <label text="Root Fe uptake (FRO2 / IRT1 / FIT)" />
      <bbox x="0.00" y="124.64" w="226.13" h="64.08" />
      <glyph id="FE_UPTAKE__u0" class="unit of information">
        <label text="reductase activity ↓ under NNMF" />
        <bbox x="6.00" y="115.64" w="217.00" h="16.00" />
      </glyph>
      <extension>
        <qbo:annotation xmlns:qbo="https://dr-richard-barker.github.io/quantum-biology-atlas/qbo/1.0" entity="QBO:FE_UPTAKE" evidenceTier="T2" confidence="verified">
          <qbo:quantumClass>structural_context</qbo:quantumClass>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT1G01580</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT4G19690</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT2G28160</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT3G56970</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT3G56980</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT1G23020</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="go_component">GO:0005886</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:evidence ref="Islam2020" doi="10.3389/fpls.2020.00325" direction="decrease" fieldRegime="NNMF">The geomagnetic field contributes to efficient iron uptake in Arabidopsis; near-null conditions affect root metal reductase activity.
</qbo:evidence>
          <qbo:evidence ref="Narayana2018" doi="10.1016/j.lssr.2018.08.005" direction="altered" fieldRegime="NNMF">Near-null magnetic field conditions affect Arabidopsis root mineral nutrition.
</qbo:evidence>
          <qbo:rationale>Carries demonstrated near-null-field evidence and NO proposed quantum route, and is classed structural_context to say so. Islam et al. measured reduced root metal reductase activity under field reduction — a real, reproducible effect with no mechanism attached. FRO2 is a flavocytochrome with FAD and two hemes, so a spin route could be argued; the review does not argue it, and no measurement supports it, so it is not claimed here.
</qbo:rationale>
        </qbo:annotation>
      </extension>
    </glyph>
    <glyph id="S_ASSIMILATION" class="complex">
      <label text="Sulfate assimilation" />
      <bbox x="260.13" y="132.96" w="226.13" h="47.44" />
      <glyph id="S_ASSIMILATION__u0" class="unit of information">
        <label text="SiR = siroheme + 4Fe-4S" />
        <bbox x="266.13" y="123.96" w="161.00" h="16.00" />
      </glyph>
      <extension>
        <qbo:annotation xmlns:qbo="https://dr-richard-barker.github.io/quantum-biology-atlas/qbo/1.0" entity="QBO:S_ASSIMILATION" evidenceTier="T2" confidence="reported">
          <qbo:quantumClass>iron_sulfur_4Fe4S</qbo:quantumClass>
          <qbo:nucleus>57Fe</qbo:nucleus>
          <qbo:nucleus>33S</qbo:nucleus>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT4G08620</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT1G78000</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT5G10180</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT3G22890</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT4G04610</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT1G62180</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT4G21990</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="agi">AT5G04590</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="ec">2.7.7.4</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="ec">1.8.4.9</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:xref db="ec">1.8.7.1</qbo:xref>
          <qbo:evidence ref="Vigani2021" doi="10.3390/ijms221810166" direction="altered" fieldRegime="NNMF">Field conditions modulate Fe-S interplay in Arabidopsis, most strongly under combined iron and sulfur deficiency.
</qbo:evidence>
          <qbo:rationale>Sulfite reductase carries a siroheme-[4Fe-4S] cofactor and is ferredoxin- dependent, so this pathway both consumes plastid reducing power and contains an Fe/S centre. It also supplies the sulfide that every cluster on QBM-04 is built from — a genuine feedback loop rather than a linear dependency.
</qbo:rationale>
        </qbo:annotation>
      </extension>
    </glyph>
    <glyph id="FE_STORAGE" class="macromolecule" compartmentRef="cell">
      <label text="Fe storage / distribution" />
      <bbox x="63.33" y="278.72" w="176.63" h="60.24" />
      <glyph id="FE_STORAGE__u0" class="unit of information">
